---
layout: product.njk
og_type: website
pagination:
  data: liveApps
  size: 1
  alias: sport
permalink: "{{ sport.downloadPage }}"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "RosterWise™ {{ sport.name }} — College {{ sport.name }} Recruiting Intelligence App | Free to Try"
  description: "RosterWise™ {{ sport.name }} lays out college {{ sport.name | lower }} rosters program by program — roster depth by {{ sport.analysisAxis }}, class-year gaps, recruiting patterns, and My RosterFit™ fit bands. {{ sport.subtext }}. Free to try; $39.99 once for full access."
  breadcrumbs:
    - text: Home
      url: /
    - text: "{{ sport.name }}"
      url: "{{ sport.hub }}"
    - text: "Get the App"
---
{% set axis = sport.analysisAxis %}
{% set verb = sport.axisVerb %}
{% set lname = sport.name | lower %}

{% import "app-macros.njk" as ap %}
{% set s = sport %}
{% set floor = sport.slug | teamFloor(previews) %}
{% set hasTours = previews[sport.slug] and previews[sport.slug].videos.length %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/app-page.css?v=2">

<!-- Hero: the Fit tour looping silently beside one App Store badge (board app-page, M3; Scott's marks, 2026-11-01) -->
<section class="product-hero ap-hero">
  <div class="ap-hero-grid">
    <div class="ap-hero-copy">
      <p class="ap-eyebrow"><img class="ap-eyebrow-icon" src="{{ sport.logo }}" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="eager">RosterWise&trade; {{ sport.name }} &middot; iPhone &amp; iPad</p>
      <h1>Find the College {{ sport.name }} Programs<br>Where Your Athlete Actually Fits</h1>
      <p class="tagline">Deep roster intelligence for college {{ lname }} recruiting families, in a dedicated {{ lname }} app.</p>
      <p class="ap-hero-cov">{{ sport.subtext }}</p>
      <div class="ap-cta">
        <div class="ap-cta-set">
          <a class="ap-badge" href="{{ sport.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
            <img src="/assets/badges/download-on-the-app-store-black.svg" alt="Download RosterWise {{ sport.name }} on the App Store" width="150" height="50">
          </a>
          {{ ap.rating(sport, "ap-rating--hero", appRatings) }}
        </div>
        <p class="ap-offer"><b>Free to try.</b> $39.99 once for full access. No subscription.</p>
        {% if hasTours %}<a class="ap-watch" href="#tours">&#9654;&ensp;Watch the three tours with sound</a>{% endif %}
        <p class="ap-hero-explore"><a href="{{ sport.hub }}">Or explore college {{ lname }} recruiting&nbsp;&rarr;</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ap-hero-media">
      {% set loopFor = false %}{% set loopHidden = false %}{% include "app-loop.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Proof: this sport's team floor (never a total across sports: Scott, board app-page-2) and the terms -->
<section class="ap-proof">
  <div class="ap-proof-inner">
    {% if floor %}<ul class="ap-stats ap-stats--one"><li><b>{{ floor }}</b><span>college {{ lname }} teams</span></li></ul>{% endif %}
    <p class="ap-terms"><span>Rosters read from each school&rsquo;s own athletics site</span><span>No login</span><span>No ads</span><span>No subscription</span></p>
  </div>
</section>

{% if hasTours %}
<!-- The three tours, each beside the questions it answers -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream ap-tours" id="tours">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="ap-tour-set" data-reels>
      {% include "app-tours.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endif %}

<!-- Try it free -->
{% set tfSports = [sport] %}{% include "app-try-free.njk" %}

<!-- The Problem -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>College {{ lname }} recruiting shouldn&rsquo;t feel like guesswork.</h2>
    <p>Families spend thousands on showcases, club fees, and recruiting services, yet still can&rsquo;t answer the most basic question: <strong>where does my athlete actually fit?</strong></p>
    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>Rosters Are Scattered</h3>
        <p>Figuring out who&rsquo;s on a {{ lname }} team means visiting hundreds of college athletics sites one by one, copying rosters into a spreadsheet, and trying to make sense of it. Nobody has time for that.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>No Real Analysis</h3>
        <p>Other tools list schools but don&rsquo;t analyze rosters. They can&rsquo;t tell you which programs have a depth gap at your athlete&rsquo;s {{ axis }}, who&rsquo;s graduating, or how your athlete compares to who&rsquo;s already there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="problem-card">
        <h3>Expensive &amp; Shallow</h3>
        <p>Recruiting services charge hundreds for generic match lists any search could produce. Real {{ lname }} roster intelligence — the kind that actually informs decisions — hasn&rsquo;t existed anywhere else.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What you'll actually see -->
<section class="product-section product-section--navy">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What you&rsquo;ll actually see</h2>
    {% for para in sport.scenario %}
    <p style="max-width: 760px;{% if not loop.first %} margin-top: 16px;{% endif %}{% if loop.last %} font-size: 1.05em; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.95);{% endif %}">{{ para | replace("'", "’") }}</p>
    {% endfor %}
    <p style="max-width: 760px; margin-top: 22px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">That&rsquo;s the difference between a list of school names and knowing <em>where the real opportunity is</em> — one picture per program, athletic and academic, built from every {{ lname }} roster so your family doesn&rsquo;t have to.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- What it analyzes -->
<section class="product-section product-section--navy">
  <div class="container">
    <h2>What RosterWise&trade; {{ sport.name }} analyzes — at every program</h2>
    <p>It goes beyond school lists. RosterWise applies <a href="/roster-intelligence/" style="color: var(--gold); font-weight: 600;">roster intelligence</a> — systematic analysis of who is actually on each {{ lname }} roster — across {{ sport.positionsExample }}.</p>

    <div class="feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Depth by {{ axis | title }}</h3>
        <p>See how every program is built by {{ axis }} — where a lineup spot is genuinely open versus stacked with returning starters.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Class-Year Gaps</h3>
        <p>Who {{ verb }} your athlete&rsquo;s {{ axis }}, and when do they graduate? A departing senior signals very different opportunity than a returning underclassman.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Physical Profile by {{ axis | title }}</h3>
        <p>How does each program build by {{ axis }}? See size and physical profiles so you know where your athlete aligns with the players already on the roster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Geographic Recruiting Patterns</h3>
        <p>What states, regions, and countries does each program recruit from? Some recruit nationally; others draw heavily from specific areas. See the pattern behind every roster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Pathway &amp; Club Analysis</h3>
        <p>What clubs, academies, and high schools did current players come from? Pathway data shows which pipelines each program draws from — and whether your athlete&rsquo;s background aligns.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Transfer Portal Activity</h3>
        <p>Does this program build through high-school recruiting or the transfer portal? A program&rsquo;s transfer pattern tells you how it fills spots — and what that means for a high-school recruit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>International Composition</h3>
        <p>What portion of the roster is domestic vs. international, and which countries are represented? This varies dramatically by division and conference — and shapes the landscape at each program.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Coach Tenure &amp; Direction</h3>
        <p>How long has the head coach been building this program? Stability tells you something about culture and direction. RosterWise includes coach tenure wherever available.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>Academic Fit &amp; School Profile</h3>
        <p>It&rsquo;s not just athletics. See school size, academic strength, graduation rates, and setting for each program — so your athlete fits in the classroom, not just on the field.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="feature-card">
        <h3>My RosterFit&trade; Personalized Scoring</h3>
        <p>Enter your athlete&rsquo;s profile — {{ sport.rosterFitProfile }} — and RosterFit checks every program on {{ sport.rosterFitFactors }}. Each factor gets a light, and each program one fit band: Strong, Good, Mixed or Weak fit. Not a generic match list. A personalized fit analysis built on real data.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Trust -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    {% if appReviews[sport.slug] %}{% set rs = sport %}{% include "app-review.njk" %}{% endif %}
    <h2>Built by a recruiting family, for yours.</h2>
    <div class="founder-section">
      <div class="founder-text">
        <p>RosterWise started with a question one recruiting parent asked another at a tournament: <em>&ldquo;How do you even figure out where your kid fits?&rdquo;</em></p>
        <p>The honest answer was: you don&rsquo;t. You visit hundreds of roster pages, take notes in a spreadsheet, and hope you&rsquo;re not missing something — or you pay a recruiting service hundreds of dollars for a list of schools you could have found yourself.</p>
        <p>We built the tool we couldn&rsquo;t find: one that goes deeper than school lists and actually analyzes rosters, surfaces opportunity, and gives families real intelligence to work with. No tool can predict recruiting outcomes — but the right data helps you ask better questions and focus your effort where it matters.</p>
        <p><strong>RosterWise is built by Grobe Games LLC.</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="product-section product-section--cream">
  <div class="container">
    <h2 style="text-align: center;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What does RosterWise {{ sport.name }} cover?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>{% if floor %}{{ floor }} college {{ lname }} teams: {% endif %}{{ sport.subtext }}. Rosters are read from each school&rsquo;s own athletics site, and every roster is labeled with its season. Each sport ships as its own dedicated app, so everything you see is {{ lname }}, with no other-sport clutter.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is RosterWise {{ sport.name }} free?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Free to try. Download the app and open three programs in full, plus one conference, and browse every program on the map and in the list before you decide. Full access is one in-app purchase of $39.99.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Is this a subscription?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Full access to RosterWise {{ sport.name }} is a one-time purchase of $39.99: no subscription, no renewals, no ads. You pay once and keep it for your athlete&rsquo;s whole recruiting journey, with each season&rsquo;s new rosters arriving in the app&rsquo;s updates.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>How current are the rosters?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Rosters are read from each school&rsquo;s own athletics site, and every roster is labeled with its season. A program whose newest roster isn&rsquo;t complete yet keeps showing its last complete one, so a half-posted roster never stands in for the real team. New rosters arrive with app updates.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do I need an account? Where does my athlete&rsquo;s information go?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No account and no login. Your athlete&rsquo;s My RosterFit&trade; profile stays on your device and in your own iCloud. It&rsquo;s never sent to us. <a href="/privacy/">Read the privacy policy.</a></p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Does it work on iPad?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. RosterWise {{ sport.name }} runs on iPhone and iPad.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>What is My RosterFit&trade;?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>A personalized fit check. Enter your athlete&rsquo;s {{ sport.rosterFitProfile }}, and RosterFit checks every {{ lname }} program on {{ sport.rosterFitFactors }}. Each factor gets a light, Strong, Moderate or Low, and each program one fit band: Strong, Good, Mixed or Weak fit. There&rsquo;s no single number, and programs are never ranked. <a href="/roster-intelligence/">Learn more about our methodology.</a></p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Will it tell me which schools will recruit my athlete?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No — and we&rsquo;re upfront about that. No tool can predict recruiting outcomes; they depend on coach communication, timing, and factors no dataset captures. RosterWise gives you the analysis to make better-informed decisions about where to focus. It&rsquo;s intelligence, not a crystal ball.</p></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>Do you offer recruiting consulting or coach outreach?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>No. RosterWise is a self-service intelligence tool, not a recruiting service — because nobody knows your athlete&rsquo;s situation better than your family.</p></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Final CTA (one App Store badge per page, in the hero: Apple's guidelines; this is a plain button) -->
<section class="product-final-cta">
  <div class="inner">
    <a href="{{ sport.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration: none; display: inline-block;">
      <img src="{{ sport.logo }}" alt="RosterWise {{ sport.name }} App" width="132" height="132" style="border-radius: 22px; box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); margin-bottom: 24px;" loading="lazy">
    </a>
    <h2>Ready to find your athlete&rsquo;s fit?</h2>
    <p>Roster intelligence for college {{ lname }}{% if floor %} across {{ floor }} teams{% endif %}: {{ sport.subtext }}. Free to try; $39.99 once for full access.</p>
    <p class="ap-final-cta"><a class="ap-btn ap-btn--gold" href="{{ sport.appStoreUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get RosterWise {{ sport.name }} free</a></p>
    <p style="margin-top: 20px; font-size: 14px;"><a href="{{ sport.hub }}" style="color: var(--gold);">Explore {{ sport.name }} &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="/app/" style="color: var(--gold);">All RosterWise apps &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <a href="/guide/" style="color: var(--gold);">Recruiting Guides &rarr;</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

<script src="/assets/app-page.js?v=2" defer></script>
